.TH tuxychart n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuxychart
.PP
A Mermaid\-style \fBxy chart\fR (bar / line) renderer for the \fBtuflow\fR diagram family. It parses a Mermaid \fBxychart\-beta\fR block into a small model and renders it to SVG or PNG with the pure\-Tcl drawing backends (\fBtclutils::tusvg\fR / \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR). No Tk, no browser, no external rasteriser.
.PP
An xy chart is not a node\-edge graph, so \fBtuxychart\fR does \fBnot\fR go through \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR; it owns its own parse and draw step, exposing the same \fBtoSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR shape the other renderers use. That lets the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR facade treat every diagram family uniformly: \fBtuflow::toPng\fR / \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR detect an \fBxychart\-beta\fR block and dispatch here (like \fBpie\fR).
.PP
Axes, gridlines, bars and line segments are drawn with the same routine on both backends, so the SVG and the raster output stay congruent.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuxychart 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuxychart::parse    text                       ;# -> model dict
::tclutils::tuxychart::toSvg    model ?-opt val ...?        ;# -> SVG string
::tclutils::tuxychart::toPng    model ?-opt val ...?        ;# -> PNG bytes
::tclutils::tuxychart::writeSvg model file ?-opt val ...?   ;# -> file (SVG)
::tclutils::tuxychart::writePng model file ?-opt val ...?   ;# -> file (PNG)
.CE
.PP
\fBparse\fR turns Mermaid \fBxychart\-beta\fR source into a model dict with keys \fBtitle\fR, \fBorientation\fR (\fBvertical\fR|\fBhorizontal\fR), \fBxtitle\fR, \fBcategories\fR (a list of axis labels), \fBxnumeric\fR/\fBxmin\fR/\fBxmax\fR (for a numeric x\-axis), \fBytitle\fR, \fByauto\fR (\fB0\fR|\fB1\fR), \fBymin\fR/\fBymax\fR, and \fBseries\fR (a list of \fB{type bar|line values {...}}\fR dicts). The render commands take that model.
.PP
Render options (all optional):
.CS
-width  N      chart width in logical px           (default 520)
-height N      chart height in logical px          (default 340)
-scale  N      raster scale, positive integer      (default 1; toPng only)
-fontfile F    real TTF/OTF for labels (raster)    (default: 6x8 bitmap font)
.CE
.PP
The SVG backend ignores \fB\-scale\fR and \fB\-fontfile\fR (it uses a fixed \fBmonospace\fR viewer font locked to the 6x8 metric). On the raster backend \fB\-scale N\fR multiplies the pixel dimensions and the font scale by \fBN\fR.
.SS "Input grammar (Mermaid \fBxychart\-beta\fR subset)"
.CS
xychart-beta                       %% header (a trailing `horizontal` is parsed)
title "<text>"                     %% chart title
x-axis "<title>"? [a, b, c, ...]   %% categorical labels
x-axis "<title>"? <min> --> <max>  %% numeric axis (labels synthesised)
y-axis "<title>"? (<min> --> <max>)?   %% axis title and/or explicit range
bar  [v1, v2, ...]                 %% a bar series   (multiple allowed)
line [v1, v2, ...]                 %% a line series  (multiple allowed)
%% ...                             %% comment, ignored
.CE
.PP
At least one \fBbar\fR or \fBline\fR series is required. Without an explicit \fBy\-axis\fR range the scale is taken automatically from the data (zero\-based, rounded up to a nice 1/2/5 ceiling).
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tuxychart
namespace import ::tclutils::tuxychart::*

set src {xychart-beta
    title "Sales Revenue"
    x-axis [jan, feb, mar, apr, may]
    y-axis "Revenue ($)" 0 --> 11000
    bar  [5000, 6000, 7500, 8200, 9500]
    line [4000, 5000, 6800, 9000, 10500]
}

set m [parse $src]
writePng $m chart.png -scale 3       ;# crisp raster
writeSvg $m chart.svg                ;# vector
.CE
.PP
Through the \fBtuflow\fR facade the same source renders without an explicit model:
.CS
package require tclutils::tuflow
::tclutils::tuflow::toPng $src -scale 3      ;# facade detects the xychart block
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Series colours come from a fixed qualitative palette (10 entries) that cycles when there are more series than colours; a legend is drawn when more than one series is present.
.IP \(bu
Multiple \fBbar\fR series share each category slot side by side; \fBline\fR series are drawn as connected segments with small square markers.
.IP \(bu
v1 limitations (honest): only the vertical orientation is drawn (a trailing \fBhorizontal\fR is recorded but ignored); the y\-axis title is placed horizontally, not rotated.
.IP \(bu
Labels use the \fBtupngdraw\fR 6x8 bitmap font by default. With \fB\-fontfile\fR on the raster backend a real outline font is used via \fBfillcontours\fR (lazy \fBGlyphs\fR, unbundled); a set\-but\-missing path is a hard error, a missing \fBGlyphs\fR package degrades silently to the bitmap font.
.IP \(bu
Companion modules: \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR and \fBtclutils::tusvg\fR (backends), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (facade / dispatch), \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (the node\-edge graph renderer for the other Mermaid types).
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUXYCHART <REASON>}\fR — \fBEMPTY\fR (no series), \fBVALUE\fR (non\-numeric value in a series), \fBARG\fR (bad render option, e.g. non\-integer \fB\-scale\fR), \fBFONT\fR (a \fB\-fontfile\fR path that does not exist).
